# Fermat's little theorem (Mathlib ZMod.pow_card, Nat.ModEq.pow_totient for
# a prime): for a prime p, a^p == a (mod p) for every a, and
# a^(p-1) == 1 (mod p) when p does not divide a.
#
# Route: the binomial theorem (x + 1)^n == sum_k C(n, k) x^k by Pascal's
# rule (bsum below), p | C(p, k) for 0 < k < p (fact.bend's
# (n + 1) C(n, k) == C(n + 1, k + 1) (k + 1) and Euclid's lemma), so
# (x + 1)^p == x^p + 1 (mod p); then induction on a. The second form
# cancels a with Euclid's lemma (no inverse needed).

# sum_{i <= k} C(n, i) x^i
def bsum(+n: Nat, k: Nat, +x: Nat) -> Nat:
  match k:
    case 0n:
      S.choose(n, 0n)
    case 1n+ +j:
      Nat.add(bsum(n, j, x), Nat.mul(S.choose(n, 1n+j), Nat.pow(x, 1n+j)))

